    ("retrieval", "easy", "What is the punishment for murder in IPC?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:302"], "IPC 302 (replaces: BNS 108) prescribes death or life imprisonment + fine (rarest of rare doctrine).", ["murder", "ipc", "302"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What is the definition of murder under IPC?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:300"], "IPC 300 defines murder as culpable homicide with 4 specific mens rea limbs, subject to 5 exceptions (provocation, sudden fight, private defence excess, consent, etc.).", ["murder", "definition", "300"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What is the equivalent of IPC Section 302 in Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita?", ["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:108", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:302"], "BNS Sec 108 replaces IPC Sec 302 verbatim — death or life imprisonment + fine for murder defined under BNS 107.", ["bns", "ipc-bns mapping", "murder"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What are the ingredients of Section 498A IPC (husband cruelty)?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:498A"], "498A requires: (a) accused is husband / relative of husband; (b) woman subjected to cruelty (willful conduct driving suicide or grave injury/harm; OR dowry harassment); (c) mental/physical cruelty included.", ["498a", "cruelty", "husband", "dowry", "arnesh kumar"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is the equivalent of IPC 498A in the new BNS 2023?", ["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:124", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:498A"], "BNS Sec 124 mirrors IPC 498A — cruelty by husband/relatives punishable up to 3 years + fine.", ["498a bns", "124 bns", "cruelty"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is Section 304B IPC (dowry death)?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:304B", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:126"], "Sec 304B deems husband/relative guilty if woman dies abnormally within 7 years of marriage, and 'soon before death' she was subjected to 498A-type cruelty for dowry demand. Min 7 years → life.", ["dowry death", "304b", "bride burning", "presumption"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is rape under IPC 375?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:375"], "IPC 375 defines rape with 4 penetrative acts (penile/oral/urethral/anal, object, manipulation, mouth) under 7 non-consent scenarios: against will, no consent, fear, impersonation, intoxication, <18, inability to consent.", ["rape", "375", "nirbhaya", "consent"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "How does the BNS 2023 change IPC 377 (unnatural offences)?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:377", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:353"], "BNS Sec 353 NARROWS 377: only carnal intercourse against the order of nature WITH A WOMAN is punished (up to 7 years + fine). It CODIFIES the Navtej Singh Johar (2018) decriminalisation for consensual adult male/female non-vaginal intercourse and same-sex private acts. Non-consensual and bestiality are penalised elsewhere.", ["377", "bns 353", "lgbtq", "navtej singh johar"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is the new BNS Sec 63 on 'false promise to marry'?", ["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:63"], "BNS 63 (2024) is a NEW OFFENCE: sexual intercourse obtained via deceitful means including false marriage promise, false employment/promotion, or identity concealment. Punishable up to 10 years + fine.", ["bns 63", "false promise to marry", "deceit", "rape by fraud"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "Explain IT Act Sec 79 safe harbour for intermediaries.", ["Information Technology Act, 2000", "79"], "IT Act 79 provides safe harbour to intermediaries (platforms) who are passive conduits, do not initiate/select/modify the transmission, and comply with 'due diligence' — now 2021 IT Rules: publish grievance officers, remove unlawful content within 36 hours of court/Govt order, appoint CCO/Nodal/RGO, etc. Loss of safe harbour on actual knowledge + failure to act, or on conspiracy/abetment.", ["79", "safe harbour", "intermediary", "it act", "due diligence"]),
    ("retrieval", "hard", "What are the eight categories of grievous hurt under IPC 320 / BNS 117?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:320", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:117"], "The 8 categories are: (1) emasculation; (2) permanent privation of sight of eye; (3) permanent privation of hearing of ear; (4) privation of any member/joint; (5) permanent impairment of any member/joint; (6) permanent facial/head disfigurement; (7) fracture/dislocation of bone/tooth; (8) any hurt endangering life OR 20 days of severe bodily pain/inability to pursue ordinary avocation.", ["grievous hurt", "320", "117 bns", "8 categories"]),
    ("retrieval", "hard", "Under PMLA Sec 3 what constitutes money-laundering?", ["Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002:3"], "Any direct/indirect involvement with PROCEEDS OF CRIME (concealment, possession, acquisition, use, projecting as untainted) — including attempt, assistance, knowing partyhood. Twin bail conditions under Sec 45. Arrest/attachment by ED Director.", ["pmla", "3", "45", "ed", "proceeds of crime", "vijay madanlal choudhary"]),
    ("retrieval", "hard", "Distinguish theft 378 from extortion 383 IPC and from robbery 390.", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:378", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:383", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:390"], "Theft = dishonest moving of movable property from possession WITHOUT CONSENT. Extortion = FEAR OF INJURY + dishonest inducement + VITIATED CONSENT to deliver property. Robbery = Theft or Extortion PLUS actual or threatened INSTANT violence/death/hurt/wrongful restraint at the time (theft: to commit/carry away; extortion: fear at presence, induce delivery then and there). 5+ conjoint robbers = Dacoity 391.", ["theft", "extortion", "robbery", "dacoity", "378 383 390"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is Dacoity? What is the punishment under IPC/BNS?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:390", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:323", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:328", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:329"], "Dacoity = 5+ persons conjointly committing/attempting robbery (IPC 391/390; BNS 324/323). Punishment: 10 years → life + fine (IPC 395 / BNS 328). Murder during dacoity = DEATH or LIFE per IPC 396 / BNS 329.", ["dacoity", "5 persons", "robbery with 5", "395 396", "328 329"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What does SCST POA Act Sec 3 cover?", ["Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989:3"], "POA Sec 3 lists caste-tinted atrocities (non-SC/ST perpetrator, SC/ST victim because of caste): Sec 3(1) common = min 6m → 5y + fine. Sec 3(2) aggravated = gang rape of SC/ST woman = DEATH or LIFE; fabricating capital evidence = LIFE; public servant perpetrator = min 1y; tonsuring/chappal garland/naked parading = 3y-7y.", ["scst act", "poa", "atrocity", "caste", "gang rape death"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What punishments exist in the BNS 2023? What's the new punishment?", ["Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:27", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:53"], "BNS Sec 27 lists: Death, Life, Rigorous, Simple, COMMUNITY SERVICE (NEW), Forfeiture, Fine. Community service (up to 100 hours) is used as an alternative for petty offences. IPC 53 had only 5 categories: Death, Life, Rigorous, Simple, Forfeiture, Fine.", ["community service", "punishments", "bns 27", "ipc 53"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "Is marital rape recognised under IPC/BNS?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:375", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:65"], "Exception 2 under IPC 375 and BNS 65 (rape definition) carves out NON-RECOGNITION of marital rape generally. BNS raised the age from 15 to 18 years — meaning a husband can be prosecuted for rape ONLY if wife is below 18, not otherwise. (The constitutional validity remains under challenge; no legislative repeal yet.)", ["marital rape", "exception 2", "age 15 to 18", "375 bns 65"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What is the domestic violence definition (PWDVA Sec 3)?", ["Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act, 2005:3", "Indian Penal Code, 1860:498A"], "DVA Sec 3 includes 4 forms of domestic violence: (1) Physical; (2) Sexual; (3) Verbal & Emotional (insults, dowry taunts, threats, etc.); (4) Economic (deprivation, dispossession, forced work). Also dowry-harassment type and threats. DVA provides civil orders (Protection/Residence/Monetary/Custody/Compensation) — breach is a criminal offence under Sec 31.", ["domestic violence", "pwdva", "3", "physical sexual verbal emotional economic"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What is the equivalent of IPC 376 rape punishment in the new BNS 2023?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:376", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:65", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:66", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:68"], "IPC 376 is replaced by BNS Sec 65 (definition) + Sec 66 (punishment = min 10 years → life + fine). Aggravated 376A/AB/B/C/D/DB become BNS 67 variants — <12 years victim = DEATH or LIFE. BNS ADDED Sec 68 Rape by Organised Crime = mandatory life or death.", ["376", "bns 66", "rape punishment", "68 organised crime death"]),
    ("retrieval", "easy", "What is the punishment for aggravated cheating (420 IPC)?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:420", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:345"], "IPC 420 / BNS 345: cheating + dishonestly inducing delivery of property OR making/altering/destroying valuable security. Punishment: up to 7 years + fine; cognizable; non-bailable.", ["420", "345 bns", "cheating", "fraud", "valuable security"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "Define culpable homicide not amounting to murder. What is the split structure?", ["Indian Penal Code, 1860:304", "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023:109"], "CHNAM occurs when a culpable homicide falls under IPC 300 exceptions (grave & sudden provocation, sudden fight, exceeding private defence, death by consent, etc.) or when the accused knows the act is 'likely' but not 'sufficient in ordinary course of nature' to kill. Punishment split: Part I (intended death/injury) → life / 10y + fine. Part II (knew risk, no intent) → 10y / fine / both.", ["culpable homicide", "chnam", "304", "109 bns", "part i part ii"]),
    ("retrieval", "hard", "What is SCST Act Sec 4 neglect of duties?", ["Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989:4"], "Sec 4 makes NON-SC/ST public servants LIABLE for WILLFUL NEGLECT of POA duties: e.g., refusing to file FIR, delaying investigation beyond 60 days, denying medical attention, failing to invoke SCST provisions. Sentence mandatory 6 months minimum → 1 year.", ["scst 4", "public servant", "willful neglect", "duties"]),
    ("retrieval", "medium", "What does PMLA Sec 45 require for bail?", ["Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002:3", "Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002:4"], "PMLA Sec 45 (post SC Vijay Madanlal 2022 reading down) imposes TWIN CONDITIONS for bail in Scheduled offences: (a) public prosecutor given opportunity to oppose; and (b) Court prima facie satisfied accused is NOT guilty of the scheduled offence AND is NOT likely to commit any offence while on bail. ED arrests; Director can attach for 180 days extendable to 365 days.", ["pmla 45", "twin conditions", "bail", "ed"]),
